  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest signal is that scvi_n200 dramatically outperforms pca_n2000 (config_049: 0.715 vs config_024: 0.629), and the current best is config_007 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat, multiprofile) at 0.721 acc. All six completed experiments use concat fusion; the effect of fusion strategy in the high-performing scvi_n200 regime is completely untested. Question: config_017 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding all other settings at their best-known values (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, multiprofile). This isolates the fusion effect as a single-variable comparison against config_007. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the cleanest exploitation of the current best direction—testing whether a learned fusion weighting can improve on simple concatenation without confounding the result with changes to encoder, aggregation, or profile setting. A positive result would yield an immediate performance gain; a null result would confirm concat sufficiency and redirect budget toward other unexplored axes (e.g., image encoder or scgpt)."
}

